# sw111, the proverb-monger (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle sw111
revision 2
state ready
dialect saltwell
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_hob_hedgecombe
written_by claude-p11-pilot
title the proverb-monger
fits stage=adult|old
prefers wealth=poor|destitute
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk quotes_old_sayings_for_everything
likes smoked_eel dice festival_bells thunder
dislikes flies haggling
fears being_found_out
hopes a_cistern_of_my_own
topics work +0.2 pastimes +0.3 lore +0.4 weather +0.2 times +0.2 prices -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# works the vines for others: quiet, unhurried, sly as a kit in a melon patch, and never without an old saying to hide behind.

words
oath! = Thorn and thistle | By the dry channel
saying! = A full jar makes no noise | The quiet vine gives the sweetest grape
proverb = A rope is worth more than a well you can't reach | Shade is borrowed, never bought | Only a fool counts another wolf's dates | Thirst teaches faster than any priest | The sand forgets every footprint but the last | A shut mouth swallows no dust
oldones = as the old ones had it | my grandfather used to say | they said it before the well was dug
trellis = the trellis-wires | the wires on the top terrace
eel = a strip of smoked eel | smoked eel off the sand-road
bones = the bones | a cup of dice
feastring = the feast-day ringing | the bells at first light on a feast
grumble_sky = thunder rolling over the dunes | a storm grumbling, and me under a roof
flies = the noon flies | the flies at the press
cistern = the old cistern out back | that cistern behind the cottages
mm = Mm | Could be | So they say
paw_full = a grape or two for the road | what falls in a pocket

any
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : They weigh my wages with one scale and their dates with another. #oldones.capitalize#, #proverb#.
opinion @2 merchants against 2 [conv.agreed_before=no] : You know my mind. A trader's thumb is never off the scale, only out of sight.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : I've picked their grapes since I was a pup. Never seen a House face on #trellis#. #mm#.
opinion @1 church against 1 : The plate goes round faster than the prayers. #proverb#.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : The well-watch see everything but what's under their own muzzles. Suits me, mostly.
opinion @1 times against 1 : A little harder each week. Nobody up the hill notices; why would they? #saying#.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : New paws take old work. There's only so many rows on #trellis#.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. #mm#. You'll be wanting something. | #greet#, #address#. Sit, if you like. Shade's free.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Early. #oldones.capitalize#, the early wolf drinks first. | #greet#. Cool while it lasts.
line @3 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Mind #trellis#; they bite. | #greet#. Talk low. The overseer has ears.
line @1 again.open : Twice in a day. #mm#. | You again. #proverb#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#. | #mm#. #greet#.
line @2 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Cool now. | #greet#. Late feet, #address#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. #saying#.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | And yours, #address#.
line @1 react.news.new : #mm#. Is that so. | #surprise#. Well, #oldones#: #proverb#.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. | Heard it. The well had it by noon.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #mm#. I'd want it from two mouths before I'd chew on it. | #doubt#. A rumour's like a mirage, #address#. Pretty from far off.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. | Bitter water. #rest#.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. Can't complain. Won't, anyway. | #mm#. Well enough. #saying#. | Poor and dry. Same as yesterday.
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. #oldones.capitalize#, #proverb#. | #sympathy#. It passes. Most things do.
line @1 decline : #hedge#. Not this one. I've a back that remembers last time. | #mm#. I'd rather not, #address#. #proverb#.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. | Fair. #proverb#.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I'll not forget it. | My thanks, #address#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. | It was nothing. #oldones.capitalize#, shade is for sharing.
line @1 preclose : #excuse#. | #mm#. The day's moving. So must I.
line @1 ack : #mm#. | #ack#.
rule @trellis_bark
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.workplace
does aside
cooldown 6h
say #saying#. | Tie and tuck. Tie and tuck. #mm#. | One for the basket. One for the basket.

rule @flies_bark
when concept=bark here.season=summer here.time=day
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #flies.capitalize#. #annoyed#. | Off. Off with you. #oath#.

rule @thunder_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Listen to it. #grumble_sky.capitalize#. | #oath#. There's a sound worth a roof.

rule @dice_bark
when concept=bark here.place=tavern
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Anyone for #bones#? Small stakes. | #bones.capitalize# want rolling. #mm#.

scene sw111_trellis
when topic=work here.region=waste self.workplace
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Retied #trellis# on the top terrace. Every knot. Nobody'll thank me. | Picked the low rows clean by noon. Clean-ish. | #oldones.capitalize#, the vine leans where the wind told it. I just tie it there.
b[job=farmer] #farm : Nobody thanks a knot. Till it slips. | Clean-ish? | My knots slip every time.
b : Long morning. | #bc_go_on# | #bc_wise#
a@farm : #proverb#. | The basket's full. That's clean enough for the overseer. | Over and under, then pull. Not under and over.
a : #saying#. | Clean enough. #mm#. | #mm#. It's only knots.

scene sw111_overseer
when topic=work|times here.region=waste self.workplace self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : They docked my day for a broken basket. A basket. #oath#. | The wages came in light again. A copper short, and a smile. | #oldones.capitalize#, the master's eye fattens the horse. Mine fattens nothing.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : Mine too. Every week a copper finds a reason to stay up there. | Count it in front of them next time. | Nor mine.
b : #bc_very_bad# | That's not right. | #bc_again#
a@poor : #proverb#. | I did. They counted it back faster. | We'll eat smiles, then.
a : #mm#. A copper here, a copper there. | It never is. #saying#. | #skint.capitalize#, and smiling about it.

scene sw111_grapes_pocket
when topic=work|food here.region=waste self.workplace here.season=summer|autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Ate a grape off the vine. Sweet as you like. Don't tell anyone. | #paw_full.capitalize#. The vines don't miss them. | A grape that falls is nobody's. #oldones.capitalize#.
b[friends] #friend : I never heard a word. | And the overseer? | #bc_ha#
b : #bc_i_know# | #bc_maybe# | Is it, now?
a@friend : Good. Nor did I. | The overseer counts baskets, not grapes. | #mm#.
a : #mm#. It was a small one. | #saying#. | #proverb#.

scene sw111_eel
when topic=food here.region=waste
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Got #eel# off a carter. Half my day's silver. Worth it. | Bread and #eel#. A meal for a wolf with no house to the name. | Nobody here eats eel but me. More for me.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : Eel! In the Waste! What's wrong with dates? | Half a day's silver on a fish? | Dates and bread, like your mother gave you.
b : #bc_lucky_you# | #surprise#. Eel? | #bc_good#
a@sw : Nothing. Dates are for every day. | #proverb#. | She gave me dates. I found eel myself.
a : Smoke and salt. The best thing that comes up the road. | #mm#. A treat's a treat. | #saying#.

scene sw111_dice
when topic=pastimes here.region=waste here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fancy #bones# tonight? Small stakes. Very small. | Won three coppers at #bones# last night. Lost two back. | #oldones.capitalize#, dice are honest; it's the paw that throws them you watch.
b[friends] #friend : Not with you. You always win. | One up, then. | I watch yours.
b : #bc_maybe# | #bc_lucky_you# | #bc_wise#
a@friend : Always? #mm#. Luck's a lucky thing. | One up. I'll take it. | #proverb#.
a : Small stakes, small sorrows. | #saying#. | #mm#. Watch away.

scene sw111_feastbells
when topic=festival|faith here.region=waste
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #feastring.capitalize#. Best sound in Saltwell. | Woke before #feastring# to hear them start. | I'd go to every feast for the bells alone. The rest, I'd skip.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : And the bread and salt after. | Before the bells? You? | And the dancing?
b : #bc_lovely# | Early, for you. | #bc_maybe#
a@sw : That too. #proverb#. | Once a year. #mm#. | Skip it. I'll stand by the wall.
a : #saying#. | #mm#. Once a year. | Bells and bread. Enough.

scene sw111_thunder
when topic=weather here.region=waste here.weather=storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Hear that? #grumble_sky.capitalize#. I could listen all night. | Thunder, and a roof over me. #oath#, that's riches. | #oldones.capitalize#, thunder's the sky clearing its throat before it speaks.
b[old] #old : My mother hid under the bed for it. | A roof's riches enough for some. | And what does it say?
b : #bc_lovely# | Loud, #address#. | #bc_go_on#
a@old : I'd lie on the roof, if they'd let me. | For some. #mm#. | Nothing that rain doesn't say better.
a : #bc_lovely# | Loud is honest. | #proverb#.

scene sw111_flies
when topic=weather|animals here.region=waste here.season=summer
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #flies.capitalize#. In my ears, in my eyes, in my bread. | Swatted forty before noon. Forty-one came. | #oldones.capitalize#, a fly is a guest nobody fed.
b[job=farmer|herder] #farm : Smoke under the eaves. Keeps the worst of them off. | They breed in the press-lees. | And never leaves.
b : #hot.capitalize# months. | #bc_very_bad# | #bc_ha#
a@farm : I'll try it. Smoke's cheap. | Then I'll curse the press-lees too. | #mm#. Never.
a : #annoyed.capitalize#. All summer. | #saying#. Not the flies, though. | #oath#. Off.

scene sw111_cistern
when topic=home|land here.region=waste self.neighbour
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's #cistern#. Nobody's. Not mine, not anyone's. | Somebody's been drawing from #cistern# again. #mm#. | #oldones.capitalize#, water belongs to the one who carries it.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : Nobody's water is everybody's quarrel. | Who? | Then carry it, and it's yours.
b : Odd. | #bc_who_q# | #bc_maybe#
a@sw : #proverb#. | I'll not say. Walls listen. | I did. Twice.
a : Odd and dry, mostly. | Somebody. #saying#. | #mm#. That's how I see it.

scene sw111_cottage
when topic=home here.region=waste self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A mat on a crowded floor. Warm, at least. | Six snores under one roof. I sleep through all of them. | #oldones.capitalize#, a crowded house is never robbed.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : Better than queueing for charity bread. | Six? I'd go mad. | Nothing in it worth robbing.
b : #bc_poor_soul# | Close quarters. | #bc_ha#
a@poor : #bc_it_is# | You'd learn. #mm#. | That too.
a : #saying#. | Close and cool. #proverb#. | #mm#. It suits me.

scene sw111_friend
when topic=friends here.region=waste self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# came in off the Saltpan white to the ears. Looked like a ghost. | #self.friend# owes me a game of #bones#. I'll collect. | I'd share my eel with #self.friend#. Half. Maybe less.
b[friends] #friend : The pan does that. | You always collect. | Half's generous, for you.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_good# | #bc_mine_too#
a@friend : It does. #proverb#. | #mm#. Always. | It is. Don't tell anyone.
a : #mm#. A salty ghost. | I will. #saying#. | #mm#. Less, probably.

scene sw111_lore_sayings
when topic=lore|smalltalk here.region=waste
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #oldones.capitalize#, #proverb#. | Do you know the one about the goat and the well? No? Good. Neither do I. | Every saying in Saltwell is older than the palms. I collect them.
b[old] #old : I taught you half of them. | There's no goat in it. It's a hen. | Older than the well, some.
b : #bc_wise# | #bc_go_on# | Collect them?
a@old : And I've kept them all. #mm#. | A hen, then. #proverb#. | Older than the well. #oath#.
a : #saying#. | #mm#. That's the joke. There isn't one. | Like coppers. They cost nothing to keep.

scene sw111_haggling
when topic=prices here.region=waste
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I won't haggle. I pay what's asked or I walk. | Watched a carter haggle a quarter-hour over a coil of rope. I'd sooner thirst. | #oldones.capitalize#, the wolf who haggles longest goes home hungriest.
b[job=merchant] #shop : Then you pay too much. | That's trade, friend. | Not in my shop.
b : #bc_fair# | #bc_ha# | #bc_wise#
a@shop : Maybe. I keep my breath. | Trade's a long word for it. | #mm#. Not in yours.
a : #mm#. I walk, mostly. | #saying#. | #proverb#.

scene sw111_times
when topic=times|prices here.region=waste world.times=hard|lean
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Bread's dearer and wages aren't. #oath#. | A little worse every week. Nobody up the hill counts it. | #oldones.capitalize#, the dry year always finds the poor house first.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : They count it. In their own favour. | Every week. | And stays longest.
b : #bc_very_bad# | #bc_true# | #bc_i_know#
a@poor : #proverb#. | #mm#. Every week. | #bc_it_is#
a : #skint.capitalize#. And smiling. | #saying#. | #mm#. It'll turn. Or it won't.

scene sw111_newcomer
when topic=newcomer here.region=waste
does tell.news / react.news / give.opinion
a : #topic.subject#'s new. Asking about work at the press already. | Saw #topic.subject# at the well. Drew first, as a guest should. | #topic.subject#, new in. #mm#. We'll see.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : Guest for three days, neighbour for good. | Good manners. | We'll see what?
b : #bc_good# | #bc_we_will_see# | #bc_maybe#
a@sw : And then a rival for my rows. #proverb#. | Manners are cheap. Work isn't. | Whether they stay.
a : #mm#. There's only so much work. | #saying#. | #oldones.capitalize#, a new broom sweeps, and an old one knows the corners.

scene sw111_faith
when topic=faith here.region=waste
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I pray when the bells ring. Easier to remember. | The Bright One hears a quiet prayer. The plate hears the loud ones. | #oldones.capitalize#, trust the Bright One, and tie your goat.
b[stage=old] #old : That's not how my grandmother told it. | Sharp tongue, for a quiet one. | And tie it tight.
b : #bc_wise# | #bc_maybe# | #bc_ha#
a@old : How did she tell it? #mm#. | #mm#. Quiet's not soft. | Tight. #proverb#.
a : #saying#. | #mm#. I'll say no more. | #oath#. Both.

scene sw111_dreams_cistern
when topic=dreams here.region=waste
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : One day I'll have a cistern with my own name cut in the lid. | If I'd a little silver put by, I'd buy a row of my own. Just one. | #oldones.capitalize#, dream at noon and you wake thirsty.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : And a lock on it. | One row's a start. | We all do.
b : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_good# | #bc_wise#
a@poor : A lock, and a dipper on a chain. | #proverb#. | #mm#. Still, I dream.
a : #someday.capitalize#. | #saying#. | #mm#. I'll dream anyway.

scene sw111_noon
when topic=day|weather here.region=waste here.time=day here.weather=clear
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #hot.capitalize#. I'll be under the press-house eaves till it breaks. | Noon. The vines sleep, so I sleep. | #oldones.capitalize#, only fools and lizards walk at noon.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : And carters. | Wise vines. | Which are you?
b : #bc_me_too# | #bc_wise# | #bc_ha#
a@sw : Carters are both. | #proverb#. | #mm#. I'm sitting.
a : #mm#. In the shade. | #saying#. | Not I. #mm#.

story the_cistern [concept=talk.memories self.age>=20]
  : When I was small I found #cistern#. Dry, full of sand, a lid on it like a millstone.
  : I dug it out with a pot, one pot a day, all one summer.
  b : And?
  : The first rain, it filled. #oath#. Since then, whoever draws from it, I count it as drawing from me.

story the_dice_carter [concept=talk.pastimes]
  : A carter once played me at #bones# for a whole eel. Laughed when I sat down.
  ask : And what did I say to that, #address#?
  b : #bc_go_on#
  : Nothing. #oldones.capitalize#, the quiet one wins. I won. Ate the eel in front of him. Slowly.

story first_thunder [concept=talk.memories]
  : First storm I remember, I was small. Every wolf in the hamlet ran for the cisterns with jars.
  : I stood in the yard and let it hit me. Thunder like the dunes falling over.
  b[old] : I remember that storm.
  b : Weren't you afraid?
  : #mm#. No. I was the only wolf in Saltwell not running. I liked it. Still do.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#, #address#. #mm#. What's wanted?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. #oldones.capitalize#, #proverb#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : #mm#. You again. Say it, then.
dlg @1 resident.job : I tie and pick at #self.workplace#. For somebody else's grapes. #saying#.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : News? #mm#. #proverb#. Nothing I'd swear to.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Mind the flies.
graft resident.hub
choice You've a saying for everything, haven't you? -> sayings
node sayings
say #mm#. The old ones had a saying for everything. I only carry them about. Like water.
free
choice Give me one, then. -> sayings_one
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node sayings_one
say #oldones.capitalize#, #proverb#. That one's free. The next costs a copper.
choice I'll keep my copper. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
